For better clarity in reference documentation, consider adding the explicit return type to the checkArgoStatus function. Additionally, when documenting examples that access external API objects, use explicit checks like 'obj != null && typeof obj === "object"' to ensure robustness against falsy values, as per repository guidelines.

```suggestion
async function checkArgoStatus(client: Cloudflare, zoneId: string): Promise<'on' | 'off'> {
  const res = await client.argo.smartRouting.get({ zone_id: zoneId });
  if (res != null && typeof res === 'object' && 'value' in res) {
    return res.value as 'on' | 'off';
  }
  return 'off';
}
```

